 ## Overview
-This method voxelize watertight models in a single GPU render pass by exploiting the Jordan curve theorem: a point is interior if a ray from it intersects the surface an odd number of times [S1]. It accumulates fragment bitmasks using bitwise XOR to determine voxel occupancy, distinguishing itself from boundary-only voxelization by producing a fully filled interior volume [S1]. It builds on [Single-pass GPU Solid Voxelization](3323-single-pass-gpu-solid-voxelization.md).
